<title>HUNGARY: Merrill Lynch says yet to choose Matav IPO listing.</title>
<headline>Merrill Lynch says yet to choose Matav IPO listing.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch said on Thursday that Hungarian telecommunications company Matav's possible international public offering would be very attractive, but it was unable to specify where the company would seek a listing.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be a very attractive offering, regardless of where it is listed,&quot; Doug Rediker, Merrill Lynch's director for central and east European Banking told Reuters.</p>
<p>Matav said on Thursday it had chosen Merrill Lynch as financial adviser and global coordinator for a potential issue.</p>
</text>
